      "title": "Nine killed and 40 injured after gunmen open fire at church funeral in Jordan",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/24/seven-killed-and-40-injured-after-gunmen-open-fire-at-church-funeral-in-jordan",
      "description": "<p>Footage broadcast on state TV shows three attackers approaching Greek Orthodox church and firing shots</p><p>Nine people have been killed after gunmen opened fire at a funeral at a church in Jordan in a rare attack ⁠on the country’s Christian minority.</p><p>Authorities described the attack on Friday as a terrorist act by extremists.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/24/seven-killed-and-40-injured-after-gunmen-open-fire-at-church-funeral-in-jordan\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-24T14:24:15"
    },
    {
      "title": "Who was behind the deadly church shooting in Jordan?",
      "link": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/24/who-was-behind-the-deadly-church-shooting-in-jordan?traffic_source=rss",
      "description": "Authorities are investigating the rare attack on a Christian church; the assailants remain unidentified and at large.",
      "source_name": "Al Jazeera All News",
      "published": "2026-10-24T13:39:26"
    },
    {
      "title": "Gunmen Open Fire at Church in Jordan, Killing at Least Seven",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/23/world/middleeast/jordan-church-shooting.html",
      "description": "Officials said the shooting, during a funeral at an Orthodox church in the southern province of Karak, was a terrorist act motivated by extremist ideology.",
      "source_name": "NYT World News",
      "published": "2026-10-23T23:07:34"
    },
    {
      "title": "India condemns attack on church in Jordan that killed 7, injured 34",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/external-affairs-defence-security/news/india-condemns-attack-on-church-in-jordan-that-killed-7-injured-34-126102400714_1.html",
      "description": "India on Saturday unequivocally condemned an attack on a church in Jordan's Karak governorate that left at least seven people dead and 34 wounded.\nNew Delhi said it stands \"firmly\" with the government and the \"friendly people\" of Jordan in \"this difficult hour\".\nSeven people were killed and 34 others sustained injuries when gunmen opened fire at a funeral in the church in Hmoud locality of Karak governorate on Friday, according to authorities in Jordan.\n\"India unequivocally condemns the heinous attack at a Church in Karak, Jordan on October 23 which resulted in the tragic loss of several innocent lives and injuries to many others,\" the Ministry of External Affairs (MEA) said.\n\"We extend our heartfelt condolences to the bereaved families and wish a swift recovery to those injured in this cowardly attack,\" it said in a statement.\n\"We also reaffirm our strong commitment to the fight against terrorism in all its forms and manifestations,\" the MEA added.\nExternal Affairs Minister S ..",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-24T10:38:59"
    },
    {
      "title": "Gunmen open fire at church during funeral in Jordan, killing 7, injuring 40",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/gunmen-open-fire-at-church-during-funeral-in-jordan-killing-7-injuring-40-126102400037_1.html",
      "description": "Gunmen opened fire during a funeral at a church in Jordan on Friday, killing seven people and wounding 40 others, authorities said.\nThe shooting took place at a Greek Orthodox church in Karak, about 180 kilometres (110 miles) south of the capital, Amman.\nFootage broadcast on Jordanian state television showed two gunmen who appear to be holding pistols approaching the church and firing shots. A third man who appears to be holding a semiautomatic rifle then approaches and opens fire, and all three then run toward the church.\nVideo footage taken by witnesses shows broken glass and pools of blood on the floor of the church.\nDorgham Halasa, who was among the mourners inside the church, said intense gunfire erupted 15 minutes after the funeral had started, and then people started running. \"It was a weird situation, and heavy gunfire,\" Halasa said.\nHe did not see the gunmen, but said other people reported seeing four of them. The Associated Press could not independently verify the number",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-24T03:04:09"
    }
  ]
